\nspawn workload selection: class=review source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:d826fb4554b9825b9cea38eb387c522977ecf69d6e6e80c0a3c63c4696a71d0b rationale="Following rank-1 recommendation: this is the Story-final candidate, so review must confirm the fuzz targets genuinely exercise production entries, the corpus covers the shapes prior reviews found, and the gate stays deterministic."\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-c34bb4, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-c34bb4)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-c34bb4, pid=4457, exit=0)\nCR revision 1 blocking finding accepted and it is the most serious defect found in this Story. CalculateObjectIdentity and VerifyObjectIdentity validate generic JSON, common-model numbers, the schema lookup and the self-field digest, but never the selected schemas closed member set or nested contract invariants. The reviewer drove both production entries with three invalid Blob Descriptors: an unknown top-level member, an unknown member inside a nested BlobChunk, and a chunk with index=9 offset=99 size=0 for a one-byte blob. All three received a digest and all three verified. For a content-addressed identity that is a bypass around the check: the system attests an object the closed contract requires the receiver to reject. Rework must add a scoped closed-shape validator for Sections 10.1-10.4 covering exact top-level and nested member sets plus chunk order, bounds and coverage, and it must be invoked on the composed production path rather than tested as an isolated helper. Separately the assigned Section 17.3 still has no scoped implementation owner and must be made traceable without claiming migration publication or atomic-reference behavior that README correctly reports unavailable.\nSTORY-260830-2wdm5e base refresh SKIPPED: the managed workspace holds uncommitted work, so there was no clean checkpoint branch to replay onto trunk e8f8e2febfbc; the branch is unchanged at fork point c9e5290b1506\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965b005 rationale="Following rank-1 recommendation: identity currently attests objects that violate the pinned closed contract, which is an attestation-integrity defect rather than a missing test."\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-186ca8, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-186ca8)\nRework closes CR revision 1 attestation bypass. Production call site prepareObjectIdentity now invokes validateImmutableObjectShape before CalculateObjectIdentity or VerifyObjectIdentity can attest. Exact Blob Descriptor/BlobChunk and recursive Transfer Manifest closed shapes refuse unknown top/nested members and chunk order/bounds/coverage violations; Section 17.3 migrated-from identity contribution is traceable without migration publication or atomic-reference claims. Final standalone gates all exited 0: focused/race/80.7% coverage, three canonical fuzz targets plus scalar fuzz at fixed 100x, scoped tracecheck for 1.6/10.1-10.4/17.3, trace tests, catalog check, full tests/coverage, vet, build, Linux/Windows cross-test builds, diff check, and board validate. Board validate retains 262 inherited MISSING_ACTIVITY diagnostics and does not list this task. Evidence: TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-results.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-logbook.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-validation-logs.tar.gz.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-186ca8, pid=53577, exit=0)\nspawn workload selection: class=review source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:d826fb4554b9825b9cea38eb387c522977ecf69d6e6e80c0a3c63c4696a71d0b rationale="Following rank-1 recommendation: Story-final candidate, so review must confirm the closed-shape validator is on the composed production path for every scoped schema, refuses without over-refusing valid objects, and that section 17.3 traceability is honest."\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-5a91c9, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-5a91c9)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-5a91c9, pid=14322, exit=0)\nCR revision 2 review returned three blocking findings and they fall into two mirror classes, so the rework must be an AUDIT rather than three spot fixes. F1 under-validates: validateMigrationExtensionObject inspects only works.relux.ax.migrated-from, so a Transfer Manifest carrying extensions with the key not_namespaced is attested by both CalculateObjectIdentity and VerifyObjectIdentity. F2 over-validates in the opposite direction: Section 1.6 bounds string[n..m] in UTF-8 CHARACTERS and ManifestEntry.target is string[1..4096], but the validator compares len(target) in bytes, so a valid 3999-character 5999-byte target is refused. Do not fix only the two fields the reviewer named. Sweep closed_shapes.go for every open or extension point and validate its full key grammar, and for every string bound switch to character counting consistent with the common scalar contract. Prove both directions at the production entries. F3 is a gate gap in the suite this candidate itself extended: the closed-shape fuzz target is defined but never invoked, so wire every defined target into the configured suite with a fixed -fuzztime.\nSTORY-260830-2wdm5e base refresh SKIPPED: the managed workspace holds uncommitted work, so there was no clean checkpoint branch to replay onto trunk e8f8e2febfbc; the branch is unchanged at fork point c9e5290b1506\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965b005 rationale="Following rank-1 recommendation: the two findings are mirror classes across the whole validator, so this needs a systematic audit of over- and under-validation rather than two point fixes."\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-9484d4, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-9484d4)\nRework revision 3 closes CR rev2 F1-F3 with a shared Section 1.6 extensions validator (full reverse-DNS grammar, 64 members, depth 4, 65536 canonical bytes), Unicode-character string bounds, and a dynamic configured-suite test requiring every repo fuzz target exactly once at fixed 100x/parallel=1. Expected-red focused tests exited 1 before the fix; all post-fix focused/full/race/coverage/four-fuzz/trace/catalog/build/vet/cross-build/JSON/diff/board gates exited 0. Coverage canonicaljson 81.2%, scalar 90.5%. task-board validate retains 262 inherited MISSING_ACTIVITY diagnostics and does not list this task. Evidence: TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev3-results.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev3-logbook.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev3-validation-logs.tar.gz.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-9484d4, pid=22190, exit=0)\nspawn workload selection: class=review source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:d826fb4554b9825b9cea38eb387c522977ecf69d6e6e80c0a3c63c4696a71d0b rationale="Following rank-1 recommendation: Story-final candidate after a two-directional validator audit; review must attack both over-refusal and under-refusal across every closed shape, not only the three previously named fields."\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-1ce05f, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-1ce05f)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=1)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-1ce05f, pid=41711, exit=1)\nspawn autonomous recovery: run RUN-260831-1ce05f queued successor RUN-260831-0a4533 (attempt 1/3, model=gpt-5.6-sol): spawned agent exited with code 1\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-0a4533)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-0a4533, pid=61816, exit=0)\nOrchestrator re-scope after CR revision 3 review. This task began as fuzz coverage and has grown, by successive review findings, into the owner of the scoped Section 10.1-10.4 closed-shape conformance gate. That growth is legitimate: three consecutive reviews proved that identity was attesting structurally invalid objects, and a fuzz task cannot honestly pass while the gate it fuzzes admits what the contract rejects. The scope field is updated to say so rather than leaving the task pretending to be narrower than it is. Splitting the work into a new task was considered and rejected because the validator is already in flight in this candidate. Method requirement for this rework: the previous two rounds each fixed exactly the fields the reviewer named and were then defeated by the next unenumerated field. Do not repeat that. Enumerate every declared constraint in the pinned Sections 10.1-10.4 systematically from SPEC.md, record the enumeration as evidence, and implement against that list. Reviewer finding F2 also stands: README claimed a completed audit that had not happened, so claims must be reproducible through both public entries or removed.\nSTORY-260830-2wdm5e base refresh SKIPPED: the managed workspace holds uncommitted work, so there was no clean checkpoint branch to replay onto trunk e8f8e2febfbc; the branch is unchanged at fork point c9e5290b1506\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965b005 rationale="Following rank-1 recommendation: two prior rounds were defeated by fixing only the named fields, so this must be a systematic derivation of every scoped constraint from the pinned specification."\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-edb7af, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-edb7af)\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-edb7af, pid=85480, exit=0)\nspawn autonomous recovery: run RUN-260831-edb7af queued successor RUN-260831-a5b476 (attempt 1/3, model=gpt-5.6-sol): Change Request construction for TASK-260830-8x76g1 failed: change_request_base_authority_mismatch: the STORY-260830-2wdm5e checkpoint fb61f3d6f5a71377de3a4938603e6cc9965cfd16 does not descend from selected authority e8f8e2febfbc75dba5fa512565b7560762855c3d\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-a5b476)\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=-1)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-a5b476, pid=18575, exit=-1)\nSTORY-260830-2wdm5e base refresh CONFLICTED against trunk e8f8e2febfbc and was aborted; the branch is unchanged at fork point c9e5290b1506 and this producer reworks on the same branch. Conflict: Auto-merging task-board.config.json\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965b005 rationale="Following rank-1 recommendation: systematic derivation of every scoped Section 10.1-10.4 constraint, now on a Story base replayed onto current trunk."\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-f460e4, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run RUN-260831-a5b476 cancelled by operator; operator action required; reason: Would hit the same base authority mismatch; refreshing the Story base first.\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-f460e4)\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=-1)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-f460e4, pid=20873, exit=-1)\nSTORY-260830-2wdm5e base refresh: the Story branch was replayed onto trunk ad7275181ca8 before this final-leaf producer started; the reviewed trunk OID is ad7275181ca8\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965b005 rationale="Following rank-1 recommendation: systematic derivation of every scoped Section 10.1-10.4 constraint, on a base that can now replay onto trunk."\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-8e0a72, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run RUN-260831-f460e4 cancelled by operator; operator action required; reason: Base still stale after conflicted replay; resolving the config collision on trunk first.\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-8e0a72)\nRevision 5 recovered the systematic Section 10.1-10.4 candidate after stale-base CR failure/rebase loss, bound CR rev3 to reviewed tree 93e6d212 and replayed the original rev4 patch stream over current Story HEAD 828d633. Independent pinned-SPEC audit fixed three over-refusals: bare strings no longer gain an undeclared non-empty bound, Section 17.3 schema_id remains a UTF-8 string, and sanitized absolute Git URLs no longer gain an undeclared path bound. Both public identity entries prove the positive boundaries. Direct gates all exited 0: focused and precision regressions, cross-platform golden, full/verbose/coverage/full-race, focused race/coverage (scalar 90.1%, canonicaljson 81.4%), four fixed-100x fuzz targets, fuzz config wiring, scoped tracecheck assigned_scopes=6, catalog, build, vet, Linux/Windows test cross-compiles and full builds, format, diff, and board validate. Board validate emitted 262 inherited MISSING_ACTIVITY diagnostics and did not list this task. Evidence: TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev5-results.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev5-logbook.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev5-validation-logs.tar.gz, updated TASK-260830-8x76g1_constraint-enumeration.md.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-8e0a72, pid=30981, exit=0)\nspawn autonomous recovery: run RUN-260831-8e0a72 queued successor RUN-260831-1c6191 (attempt 1/3, model=gpt-5.6-sol): Change Request construction for TASK-260830-8x76g1 failed: change_request_base_authority_mismatch: the STORY-260830-2wdm5e candidate provenance disagrees (selected=ad7275181ca82fc3fa29544e3893923a92d7b9d5 current=ad7275181ca82fc3fa29544e3893923a92d7b9d5 checkpoint=fb61f3d6f5a71377de3a4938603e6cc9965cfd16 branch=828d63321a74bb6be1b322eebc5ea64794d7d914 head=828d63321a74bb6be1b322eebc5ea64794d7d914)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-1c6191)\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=-1)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-1c6191, pid=50463, exit=-1)\nWorkspace recovery, disclosed in full. The managed workspace hit the base-refresh provenance defect: a replay rewrote the Story branch while the record kept the pre-replay checkpoint OID, and provisioning then refused with worktree_stale. The supported re-provision path does not self-heal that, and hand-editing the private record was rejected, so the workspace and branch were discarded after preserving every byte. Nothing is lost and nothing is unreviewed. The two already-accepted leaves are attached verbatim as TASK-260830-8x76g1_accepted-leaves-tree.tar.gz, extracted from signed checkpoint 828d633 whose tree is 6b400c3c6b0718d4d08dc905ac46673bd4a87aa6; TASK-260830-1pbx0c CR revision 6 and TASK-260830-236x9n CR revision 5 were accepted on exactly that content and both tasks remain done. This leafs own in-flight audit work is attached as TASK-260830-8x76g1_audit-rework-carryforward.tar.gz. Restore both verbatim rather than re-deriving them, then finish the outstanding rework: the systematic Section 10.1-10.4 constraint derivation from the pinned SPEC.md, the forgeable-extension-key and character-bound classes in both directions, and honest README claims. The Story candidate is story_final and carries the whole Story delta, so the final review sees all three leaves in one candidate; re-checkpointing the earlier leaves is neither required nor intended.\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965b005 rationale="Following rank-1 recommendation: restore the accepted leaf content verbatim and complete the systematic scoped-constraint derivation on a freshly