+# TASK-260830-8x76g1 developer results — RUN-260901-64187f
+
+## Outcome
+
+This revision is test-only, as required by the CR revision 11 verdict. It adds
+public-entry boundary proofs in `internal/canonicaljson/boundary_constraints_test.go`.
+No production implementation, pinned specification, README, catalog, or validation
+configuration was changed by this run.
+
+The table-driven production-entry test now carries accept-at-bound and
+refuse-past-bound cases for all 15 rev11 findings through both
+`CalculateObjectIdentity` and `VerifyObjectIdentity`:
+
+- BlobChunk size 4,194,304; GitIndex version lower edge 2; GitIndexEntry mode
+  uint32; Board Identity logical ID 128 characters; managed-tree project config
+  paths 256; GitSubmodule repository identity 256 characters; initialized
+  GitSubmodule project config paths 256.
+- Non-empty task element ID, board goal ID, argv element, managed-tree identity,
+  Git workspace repository identity, Git remote name, GitSubmodule repository
+  identity, and WorkspaceSnapshot members.
+
+Three additional cases make the whole bound-expression sweep meaningful rather
+than list-shaped: media-type type/subtype case are attacked independently,
+extension object depth is attacked independently of array depth, and a
+zero-size BlobChunk is attacked together with the empty-descriptor invariant.
+
+The existing GitIndex.entries disclosure remains exact: the direct validator
+accepts 65,536 and refuses 65,537 entries; the valid 65,536-entry parent encodes
+to 12,323,001 bytes, so both public entries refuse it at the 5,242,880-byte outer
+identity cap.
+
+## Mutation evidence
+
+The attached rev11 batches 1 through 7 were invoked on the final test tree. The
+original harness contains stale line metadata for regex, BlobChunk-zero, and
+extension-object-depth rows; these rows truthfully produced `SETUP-FAIL` and
+were rerun with corrected line bindings. One accidental invocation used
+`mutate2.py` for single-edit batch3 and exited 1 with `KeyError: edits`; the
+correct `mutate.py` invocation was then run and exited 0.
+
+All 15 rev11 findings are killed. Batch6 reconfirmed all seven upper-bound
+findings against `./...`; the three independent lower-bound sites are killed
+directly, and the five `requireBoundedString(..., 1, ...)` sites are killed by
+combined mutants that remove the shared `requireString` non-empty enforcement
+as well as widening the parameter. This is necessary because a one-site
+`1 -> 0` edit is behaviorally equivalent while `requireString` still refuses
+empty text.
+
+The final effective sweep has zero actionable survivors and zero setup
+failures. Raw one-site `SURVIVED` rows are exactly the redundant checks already
+classified by the reviewer plus the shared-non-empty cases above; their
+multi-site widening variants are killed. BlobChunk.index's uint32 ceiling is
+subsumed by `index == array position` and the public object-size cap, matching
+the rev11 reviewer classification rather than inventing an unreachable public
+fixture.
+
+Detailed sweep accounting is in
+`TASK-260830-8x76g1_run-RUN-260901-64187f-mutation-sweep.md`.
+
+## Direct validation
+
+Every command below was run as a standalone foreground process.
+
+| Command | Exit | Result |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| `test -z "$(gofmt -l $(git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard -- '*.go'))"` | 0 | formatted |
+| `git diff --check` | 0 | clean |
+| `go build ./...` | 0 | builds |
+| `go vet ./...` | 0 | clean |
+| focused boundary tests | 0 | 40 public-entry boundary pairs plus GitIndex exception |
+| `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -count=1 -v` | 0 | pass |
+| `go test ./... -count=1 -v` | 0 | pass |
+| `go test ./... -race -count=1` | 0 | pass |
+| `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 | canonicaljson 83.4%, scalar 90.1%, traceability 85.0% |
+| scalar fuzz, fixed `100x`, `-parallel=1` | 0 | 100 executions |
+| canonical round-trip fuzz, fixed `100x`, `-parallel=1` | 0 | 100 executions |
+| identity representation fuzz, fixed `100x`, `-parallel=1` | 0 | 100 executions |
+| closed-shape refusal fuzz, fixed `100x`, `-parallel=1` | 0 | 100 executions |
+| full `tracecheck` | 0 | 60 contracts, 36 normative sections |
+| scoped `tracecheck -section 17.3` | 0 | assigned scopes 1 |
+| scoped `tracecheck` for 1.6, 10.1-10.4, 17.3 | 0 | assigned scopes 6 |
+| catalog generator `-check` | 0 | generated catalog current |
+| `GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 | cross-build pass |
+| `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 | cross-build pass |
+| JSON parse of config and all `internal/**/*.json` | 0 | 5 files parsed |
+| `task-board validate` | 0 | 262 inherited `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics; this task not listed |
+
+The first archive comparison probe exited 127 because a zsh loop variable named
+`path` overwrote zsh's special `$path` array and removed commands from `$PATH`.
+It made no repository changes. The corrected probe used `item` and absolute
+`/usr/bin/cmp`, exited 0, and verified the supplied archive SHA-256 digests.
+
+The package is read-only; durable-state crash/idempotency recovery is not
+applicable. No new capability is advertised.
