+
+Three additional cases make the whole bound-expression sweep meaningful rather
+than list-shaped: media-type type/subtype case are attacked independently,
+extension object depth is attacked independently of array depth, and a
+zero-size BlobChunk is attacked together with the empty-descriptor invariant.
+
+The existing GitIndex.entries disclosure remains exact: the direct validator
+accepts 65,536 and refuses 65,537 entries; the valid 65,536-entry parent encodes
+to 12,323,001 bytes, so both public entries refuse it at the 5,242,880-byte outer
+identity cap.
